    "answer": "Based on the provided query results and historical data from January to February 2000, here are the asset class recommendations for USD appreciation and depreciation:\n\nWhen USD is appreciated (2000-01-04 onwards):\n1. Large-cap stocks (e.g., S&P 500): Show strong performance during USD appreciation periods\n2. NASDAQ: Demonstrates resilience in volatile USD environments with consistent growth\n\nWhen USD is depreciated (January 10, 2000 onwards):\n1. Foreign Stocks: Exhibit higher returns during USD depreciation phases due to currency hedging effects\n2. Emerging Markets: Provide opportunities for diversification through currency diversification strategies\n\nKey Observations:\n- The data suggests that large-cap stocks and NASDAQ tend to perform better during USD appreciation periods\n- However, foreign stocks and emerging markets can offer diversification benefits when the USD is depreciated\n\nRecommendations:\n1. During USD appreciation (e.g., 2000-01-04 onwards):\n   - Consider allocating more funds to S&P 500 or Nasdaq-listed companies for their historical stability during USD strength\n   - Include foreign stock exposure through currency hedges as a diversification strategy\n\n2. During USD depreciation (January 10, 2000 onwards):\n   - Focus on international equities with strong currency hedging strategies\n   - Invest in emerging markets to capture potential growth opportunities outside the USD zone\n\nNote: These recommendations are based on historical data and may not reflect current market conditions or future trends.",
